# Line endings: always LF in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# The dev container is Linux, but on a laptop it runs the files straight from
# the host checkout. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which turns
# LF into CRLF on checkout; bash then reads the trailing \r as part of the
# command (e.g. "set: pipefail: invalid option name") and bootstrap.sh fails.
# eol=lf overrides each contributor's autocrlf setting. Linux, macOS and
# Codespaces already use LF, so nothing changes there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
